From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 4evy <git@evy.pink>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 1970 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] git fetch: refresh state after shallow boundary
 changes

Expose the existing fetch depth plumbing to the CLI. Allow an existing
shallow repository to take its depth from configuration.

When Git changes the shallow boundary, refresh the backend caches before
importing refs and invalidate the persisted commit index after the
transaction. This lets the next repository load rebuild ancestry using
the new boundary.
---
